Set XDG_SEAT and XDG_VTNR before opening the PAM session, so pam_systemd
registers the session on seat0. Without a seat, logind never marks the
session as active on a seat, which e.g. disables Bluetooth in WirePlumber
and device ACLs from udev.

Minimal backport of the seat part of
https://github.com/coastalwhite/lemurs/commit/7283f01e38, which does not
apply to 0.4.0.
See https://github.com/coastalwhite/lemurs/issues/256

